{
  "item": "GloveMale05",
  "mu_name": "Bone Gloves",
  "mu_name_from": "MuMain maps MODEL_HELM + i to HelmMale{i+1}, so file 05 is armour index 4, which openmu names Bone. Not Plate - Plate is index 9, file 10.",
  "profile": "armour",
  "stats": {
    "note": "The item's own row, copied from OpenMU's 0.75 initialiser rather than restated, with the call it came from beside it.",
    "from": "openmu/src/Persistence/Initialization/Version075/Items/Armors.cs. The 0.75 table, which is the version this server is being built to.",
    "call": "CreateGloves(4, \"Bone Gloves\", 14, 5, 0, 30, 20, 0, 1, 0, 0)",
    "call_note": "ArmorInitializerBase.CreateGloves(number, name, dropLevel, defense, attackSpeed, durability, strengthRequirement, agilityRequirement, darkWizardClassLevel, darkKnightClassLevel, elfClassLevel). Slot 5, so `armor.Group = (byte)(slot + 5)` makes the group 10.",
    "group": 10,
    "number": 4,
    "drop_level": 14,
    "drops_from_monsters": true,
    "slot": 5,
    "width": 2,
    "height": 2,
    "defense": 5,
    "defense_note": "Points of defence, in the row and summed into Player.ArmourDefense by Wear - see shared/Rows.cs.",
    "attack_speed": 0,
    "durability": 30,
    "requires": {
      "level": 0,
      "strength": 20,
      "agility": 0,
      "energy": 0,
      "vitality": 0
    },
    "classes": [
      "wizard"
    ],
    "classes_from": "The last three ints of the call are 1, 0, 0 - the Dark Wizard alone.",
    "shelf_note": "On Pasi's shelf at +2, the middle column of the mage's stock - see shared/Market.cs."
  },
  "sheets": [
    "gloves_06.png",
    "hide.png"
  ],
  "blocked_was": "This asset carried a `blocked` note saying the pipeline handled one sheet per asset. That was true when it was written and is not now - ArmorMale10 wears upper_11 and hide, GloveMale06 wears gloves_07 and hide, and both are built - so the note is gone and the piece goes down the same path they did.",
  "material_note": "Bone, and not the profile's plate_steel, which is what this set was built with and is the fault behind 'the bone set seemed dark'. MU paints these five sheets dark - upper_06 means 83 and lower_06 means 57 against the Plate set's 137 - and a dark albedo declared metallic 1.0 has no diffuse term to carry its mid-tones, so the armour kept the drawn highlights and went black between them. Nothing here was forged: it is skull, rib and claw over a dark hide. See materials/bone.json, which argues the number and the case against reusing chitin. Twenty-two islands for 156 triangles, which is the two gauntlets' fingers each an island of one to four triangles. All gloves_06 or hide, all plate.",
